The TypeScript adaptation sizes the per-channel ring at delay + 1 samples instead
of native's power-of-two ring of sample_rate * COMP_DELAY_MAX_DELAY samples (the
output is identical), declares that ring as reserved state bounded by the frame
allocation limit, and refuses expressions, non-integer values for the integer
options, timeline enable and runtime commands instead of implementing them.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
